## Assistant (Spring AI)

Chat model: **<%= providers[ai.chat] %>**<% if (ai.store !== "none") { %>; notes in **<%= ai.store %>**, embedded with
**<%= providers[ai.embeddings] %>** (<%= ai.dimensions %> dimensions)<% } %>.

<% if (ai.chat !== "ollama" || (ai.embeddings && ai.embeddings !== "ollama")) { -%>
1. `cp apps/api/.env.example apps/api/.env` and fill in the API key (the file is git-ignored).
<% } -%>
<% if (ai.ollama) { -%>
1. `docker compose up -d` starts Ollama; the API downloads its models on first start (minutes, a few GB).
<% } -%>
<% if (ai.store !== "none") { -%>
1. `POST /api/assistant/notes` `{"title", "text"}` teaches it something; only you get answers from your notes.
<% } -%>
1. `POST /api/assistant/answers` `{"question"}` → `{"answer", "sources"}`<% if (config.reactive) { %>, or
   `POST /api/assistant/answers/stream` for Server-Sent Events while the model writes<% } %>.

<% if (ai.store !== "none") { -%>
When nothing in your notes is close enough (`app.assistant.min-similarity`), the model is not asked. Changing
the embeddings model changes the vectors' size: <%= ai.store === "pgvector" ? "a new migration, and" : "a new index, and" %> embedding the notes again.
The tests use fake models against the real store: they need Docker, never a key.
<% } else { -%>
The tests use a fake model: they never need a key or the network.
<% } -%>
<% } -%>
